          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Reprint 2026-27"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "header",
          "index": 1,
          "bbox": [
            0.562,
            0.047,
            0.847,
            0.064
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Expressions Using Letter-Numbers"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 2,
          "bbox": [
            0.11,
            0.085,
            0.826,
            0.11
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "？ How much should she pay if she buys 10 coconuts and 5 kg jaggery?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 3,
          "bbox": [
            0.175,
            0.117,
            0.474,
            0.136
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Cost of 10 coconuts = 10 × ₹35"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 4,
          "bbox": [
            0.175,
            0.136,
            0.465,
            0.155
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Cost of 5 kg jaggery = 5 × ₹60"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "index": 5,
          "bbox": [
            0.175,
            0.155,
            0.68,
            0.174
          ],
          "image_path": "images/page_2_equation_5.jpg",
          "content": "Total cost  = 10 \\times \\bar{x}35 + 5 \\times \\bar{x}60 = \\bar{x}350 + \\bar{x}300 = \\bar{x}650."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 6,
          "bbox": [
            0.11,
            0.182,
            0.815,
            0.207
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "？ How much should she pay if she buys 8 coconuts and 9 kg jaggery?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 7,
          "bbox": [
            0.109,
            0.224,
            0.848,
            0.266
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "？ Write an algebraic expression to find the total amount to be paid for a given number of coconuts and quantity of jaggery."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 8,
          "bbox": [
            0.174,
            0.274,
            0.811,
            0.294
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Let us identify the relationships and then write the expressions."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "index": 9,
          "bbox": [
            0.184,
            0.304,
            0.814,
            0.45
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "table_body",
              "index": 9,
              "bbox": [
                0.184,
                0.304,
                0.814,
                0.45
              ],
              "image_path": "images/page_2_table_9.jpg",
              "content": "<table><tbody><tr><td>Quantity needed</td><td>Relationship</td><td>Expression</td></tr><tr><td>Cost of coconuts</td><td>Number of coconuts × 35</td><td>c × 35</td></tr><tr><td>Cost of jaggery</td><td>Number of kgs of jaggery × 60</td><td>j × 60</td></tr></tbody></table>"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 10,
          "bbox": [
            0.15,
            0.461,
            0.847,
            0.5
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Here, ‘c’ represents the number of coconuts and ‘j’ represents the number of kgs of jaggery. The total amount to be paid will be:"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 11,
          "bbox": [
            0.33,
            0.503,
            0.667,
            0.524
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Cost of coconuts + Cost of jaggery."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 12,
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.527,
            0.733,
            0.548
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "The corresponding algebraic expression can be written as:"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "index": 13,
          "bbox": [
            0.43,
            0.551,
            0.571,
            0.572
          ],
          "image_path": "images/page_2_equation_13.jpg",
          "content": "c \\times 35 + j \\times 60"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 14,
          "bbox": [
            0.11,
            0.586,
            0.847,
            0.627
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Use this expression (or formula) to find the total amount to be paid for 7 coconuts and 4 kg jaggery."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 15,
          "bbox": [
            0.15,
            0.635,
            0.847,
            0.673
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Notice that for different values of ‘c’ and ‘j’, the value of the expression also changes."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 16,
          "bbox": [
            0.174,
            0.673,
            0.666,
            0.693
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Writing this expression as a sum of terms we get:"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "index": 17,
          "bbox": [
            0.411,
            0.695,
            0.588,
            0.717
          ],
          "image_path": "images/page_2_equation_17.jpg",
          "content": "\\boxed { \\quad c \\times 3 5 \\quad } + \\quad \\boxed { \\quad j \\times 6 0 \\quad }"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 18,
          "bbox": [
            0.11,
            0.723,
            0.847,
            0.764
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "？ "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Example 4:",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " We are familiar with calculating the perimeters of simple shapes. Write expressions for perimeters."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 19,
          "bbox": [
            0.149,
            0.768,
            0.847,
            0.808
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "The perimeter of a square is "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "4 times the length of its side",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": ". This can be written as the expression: "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "4 × q",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": ", where q stands for the sidelength."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 20,
          "bbox": [
            0.11,
            0.814,
            0.847,
            0.855
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "？ What is the perimeter of a square with sidelength 7 cm? Use the expression to find out."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 21,
          "bbox": [
            0.15,
            0.864,
            0.849,
            0.904
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "You must have realised how the use of letter-numbers and algebraic expressions allows us to express general mathematical relations in"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "page_number",
